Changes made by Alola Inc. to the upstream source:
  - Module path and package renamed to github.com/alolainc/anet.
  - Layout: the poller (upstream poll_*.go, fd_operator*.go, sys_epoll_*.go) moved to internal/netpoll, the
    socket system calls (upstream sys_*.go, net_io.go) to internal/socket, the error values to internal/errs and
    the logger to internal/logging. Package anet re-exports the public names, so its API is unchanged.
    Upstream anet_unix.go and anet_windows.go were merged into anet.go, which delegates to a platform backend
    (backend*.go).
  - internal/runner uses github.com/alolainc/gopool to run connection callbacks.
  - Log prefix changed to "[anet]:".
  - internal/netpoll/poller.go (upstream poll_default.go): readall no longer spins on EAGAIN/EINTR.
  - internal/netpoll/poller_bsd.go (upstream poll_default_bsd.go): fixed the value reported in the readall
    error log; the wake-up event moved to waker_kqueue.go, and waker_pipe.go (new) wakes the poller with a
    self-pipe on OpenBSD, NetBSD and DragonFly, which upstream did not build on.
  - internal/socket/sendmsg_bsd.go: Msghdr.Iovlen is set per platform (iovlen_*.go), as it is a uint32 on
    OpenBSD.
  - connection_impl.go: the input buffer is no longer allocated in connection init; it is allocated
    on the first read, so idle connections do not hold a buffer each.
  - Added WithInlineRequest and WithGoroutineRequest: OnRequest runs on the poller goroutine by default (not
    when OnConnect is set); WithGoroutineRequest restores a goroutine per request. Inline mode raises the
    poller count to GOMAXPROCS when the user did not choose it (internal/netpoll/manager.go). Touches
    connection_impl.go, connection_onevent.go, connection_reactor.go, options.go and errors.go (new
    ErrNotEnoughData).
  - Added SocketTuner (SO_SNDBUF, SO_RCVBUF, TCP_NOTSENT_LOWAT) with WithSendBuffer, WithRecvBuffer and
    WithNotSentLowat.
  - Added package tee (fan-out of frames to many connections) and PendingWrite on the connection types.
  - System calls use golang.org/x/sys/unix instead of package syscall (Linux 32-bit now builds).
  - nocopy_linkbuffer.go: dropIfDrained gives a drained buffer's memory back to the pool; connections call it
    after an inline OnRequest (input) and after a complete Flush (output), so idle connections hold no buffers.
    The flush barrier is taken from the pool per call.
  - connection_impl.go, connection_reactor.go: the output buffer has one owner at a time (writer or poller),
    which fixes concurrent Flush calls racing with the poller in inline mode.
  - Added PacketLoop (packet*.go, internal/socket/recvfrom.go): UDP served by the pollers.
  - Added WithReusePort and CreateReusePortListener (SO_REUSEPORT on Linux, SO_REUSEPORT_LB on FreeBSD, a
    listener shared by the pollers elsewhere). server.Close is split so a shared listener is closed once.
  - internal/socket: sockets and accepted connections are close-on-exec and non-blocking atomically
    (SOCK_CLOEXEC, accept4) where the kernel supports it, else under syscall.ForkLock; upstream left accepted
    descriptors inheritable by exec'd children.
  - Added Config.Logger (*slog.Logger).
  - portable_conn.go, portable_server.go, backend_portable.go (new, Alola Inc.): a net.Conn based backend
    used on Windows, where anet has no native poller.
